  "notes": "The research flags this pair as the odd one out in the Bay lane — 60s Stax/soul sources rather than 70s P-Funk, giving `I–vi–IV–V`-family soul cycles that are major-leaning. So this is one of only three entries in the batch with major key spellings and a `major`-led scale list, and the only one in the Bay half. The rest of the model is deliberately unelaborate because the research says so: a single sampled horn or reed figure looped over 4 bars, minimal overdubbing, sung backing vocals on the hook. That is one motif at 2–5 notes a bar with a high `chordToneBias`, `timbreHint` `horn_stab`, a countermelody at 0.35 for the backing voices, and no arrangement bridge — the record is short and has none. The kit is sample-derived with an added sub kick and swung 16ths, which is a mid kick density with the swing pushed to 0.62, the heaviest in this batch. The bass walks with moderate melodic movement, so `followRootsProb` sits at 0.5 with major-mode passing tones (`M3`, `M6`) rather than the blue thirds every minor-mode entry here uses. ⚠ `medium` is the research's own rating: the sample flip is documented in detail, the drum and bass numbers are read from the single record the pair is known for.",
